# What `macconfig-check.sh --fix` may repair on its own. One row per issue id; the checks tag every
# drift / warning with one of these ids (`fixid <id>` in checks/*.sh). The single place the
# safe / needs-Paul split lives — tests/autofix.test.sh keeps it in sync with macconfig-check.sh.
# Format (pipe-delimited): id | class | fixer | what it covers / why
#   class:  SAFE = reversible preference write, applied automatically by --fix
#           PAUL = report only, never automated (listed under "Needs Paul")
#   fixer:  SAFE rows only — the macconfig-check.sh fix routine that reuses an existing setter:
#             macos        macos.sh --only … (backs up the domain first; restarts Dock /
#                          Finder / SystemUIServer / ControlCenter only if a value changed;
#                          "logout" rows are reported as needing a logout). Dock rows, including
#                          minimize-to-application and no-bouncing, use restart Dock.
#             launchagent  scripts/install-launchagent.sh (render @HOME@ -> $HOME),
#                          then scripts/load-launchagent.sh. Bootstrap only if the
#                          job isn't loaded. If the installed plist differs from
#                          the rendered repo copy, rewrite it and bootout/bootstrap.
#             symlink      ln -sfn to the repo source, ONLY if the target is a symlink or
#                          missing — a real file is never overwritten
#             hammerspoon  open -g -a Hammerspoon (only if installed and not running)
#             desktop      lib/desktop-bindings.py --apply (backs up com.apple.spaces,
#                          writes app-bindings, restarts Dock only if a pin changed)
#             fileext      lib/file-handlers.py --apply (duti -s BUNDLE .ext all).
#                          An extension whose only UTI is dyn.* (duti error -50)
#                          is skipped with a warning. It is not drift.
# An id that isn't listed here is treated as PAUL ("not classified").
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored.

# ---- SAFE: applied automatically by --fix ----
defaults|SAFE|macos|macOS default from lib/macos-defaults.list (Dock icon size / recents / minimize into app / no bouncing — restart Dock, Finder, Trash, Screenshots, Spaces, menu bar, Trackpad, window tiling, Stage Manager, desktop widgets, …)
dictation-164|SAFE|macos|dictation hotkey 164 re-pinned by scripts/pin-dictation-hotkey-164.sh
quicknote-190|SAFE|macos|Quick Note hotkey 190 (Globe/Fn+Q) disabled by scripts/pin-quicknote-hotkey-190.sh
spotlight-64|SAFE|macos|Spotlight hotkey 64 (Command+Space) restored by scripts/pin-spotlight-hotkey-64.sh when it differs. No LaunchAgent. The script runs activateSettings -u
finder-icon-view|SAFE|macos|Finder icon view 72/13 and Sort By Name (arrangeBy=name) re-pinned by scripts/pin-finder-icon-view.sh. Desktop view is not written
finder-recents|SAFE|macos|Finder sidebar Recents hidden by lib/finder-sidebar-recents.py
finder-show|SAFE|macos|Finder menu shortcut Show Finder set to Cmd-Ctrl-Shift-F (NSUserKeyEquivalents, -dict-add)
titlebar-double-click|SAFE|macos|delete AppleMiniaturizeOnDoubleClick when it is set, so double-click fills the window (AppleActionOnDoubleClick Fill is the defaults row)
coteditor|SAFE|macos|CotEditor theme + monospaced font (macos.sh)
launchagent|SAFE|launchagent|repo LaunchAgent rendered from launchagents/ (@HOME@ -> $HOME) and loaded; a plist that differs from the repo is rewritten and reloaded with launchctl bootout then bootstrap
symlink|SAFE|symlink|repo-managed symlink re-pointed (only if the target is a symlink or missing)
hammerspoon|SAFE|hammerspoon|Hammerspoon started (open -g -a Hammerspoon)
desktop-assign|SAFE|desktop|Dock Assign To pins from lib/desktop-bindings.list (com.apple.spaces app-bindings; Desktop N is the current Main-display Space UUID; none deletes the key; an @APP@ path reads CFBundleIdentifier and a missing app is not written; restarts Dock)
file-handler|SAFE|fileext|Finder double-click defaults from lib/file-handlers.list (duti -s BUNDLE .ext all; an extension with only a dyn.* UTI is skipped, not drift)
display-more-space|SAFE|macos|Built-in display More Space. macos.sh runs displayplacer for the built-in panel only (14" 1800x1169, 16" 2056x1329 from lib/display-resolution.list), keeping the current refresh rate when that scaled mode exists. External displays are repeated unchanged. A missing displayplacer or a missing mode stays the manual step (System Settings → Displays)

# ---- PAUL: report only, never automated ----
brew|PAUL||installing / uninstalling / updating apps — brewsync (the routine runs it separately)
app-install|PAUL||an app is missing — install it (Brewfile / brewsync, or Fleet Self service)
developer-folder|PAUL||~/Developer is missing — install.sh creates it
unwanted-app|PAUL||uninstalling apps needs sudo — prune-apps.sh
dock-apps|PAUL||Dock app layout — dock.sh rebuilds the whole Dock; run it if the change is unwanted
login-shell|PAUL||login shell change needs sudo / chsh — shell.sh
hostname|PAUL||hostname change needs sudo — hostname.sh
auto-brightness|PAUL||Automatically adjust brightness — System Settings → Displays. Readable without sudo via corebrightnessdiag; the saved CoreBrightness plist is root-owned and its keys move between macOS versions, so --fix never writes it. True Tone and battery dim are left alone
ac-sleep|PAUL||Power — sudo pmset for AC sleep 0, AC display sleep 10, battery display sleep 2, and AC wake for network access (manual step ac-sleep). pmset -g custom is readable without sudo; --fix never runs sudo. Battery idle sleep is not changed. Closing the lid still sleeps the Mac
notifications|PAUL||Allow Notifications for apps in lib/notifications-off.list, and Hammerspoon notification style Alerts — System Settings → Notifications. Read from the usernoted group plist; --fix never writes it
url-handler|PAUL||default-app changes can raise a macOS confirmation dialog — handlers.sh
app-config|PAUL||an app config in the repo is invalid or overridden — fix ghostty/config, or merge and remove the override by hand
logi-settings|PAUL||a Logi Options+ setting (MX Master 3S) drifted from lib/logi-expected.list — set it back in the app; settings.db is never written
logi-unreadable|PAUL||Logi Options+ settings.db missing or in an unreadable format — open the app once, or update lib/logi-settings.py
modes-config|PAUL||hammerspoon/modes.lua invalid or state.json unreadable — fix modes.lua and reload Hammerspoon / switch to Normal from the menu bar
modes-setup|PAUL||a Focus mode or Focus Shortcut named in modes.lua is missing — create it (manualsteps open)
mode-long|PAUL||a non-Normal mode has been on longer than HEALTH_MODE_MAX_HOURS — switch back from the menu bar (never switched automatically)
karabiner-rules|PAUL||karabiner.json is a repo file — restore it from git (dotfiles git state)
karabiner-background|PAUL||Karabiner-Core-Service and Karabiner-VirtualHIDDevice-Daemon enabled and allowed (the same records sfltool dumpbtm prints). Check-only: --fix never changes Login Items. Karabiner-Elements Privileged Daemons v2 may stay disabled
repo-file|PAUL||a repo script is missing — restore it from git (dotfiles git state)
login-items|PAUL||login items — ChatGPT stays off. Tailscale stays in Open at Login (System Settings → General → Login Items & Extensions → under Open at Login click + → Applications → Tailscale → Open). Check-only: --fix never adds or removes a login item
tcc|PAUL||privacy permission (TCC) — System Settings → Privacy & Security
manual-step|PAUL||manual step (permission / sign-in) — manualsteps open
mouse-settings|PAUL||Mouse tracking speed (NSGlobalDomain com.apple.mouse.scaling = 1.5, 7th notch from Slow) and scrolling speed (com.apple.scrollwheel.scaling = 0.5, 5th notch from Slow) — System Settings → Mouse. Check-only: writing these is unreliable on recent macOS, so --fix never writes them. Double-click and secondary click stay in the manual step
pointer-size|PAUL||Pointer size one notch above Normal (com.apple.universalaccess mouseDriverCursorSize, about 1.4; accept 1.2-2.0) — System Settings → Accessibility → Display → Pointer. Check-only (manual step pointer-size): --fix never writes it
input-british|PAUL||British keyboard layout only (com.apple.HIToolbox AppleEnabledInputSources and AppleSelectedInputSources, KeyboardLayout Name British). Other entries that are not a keyboard layout, such as Press and Hold, are fine. Check-only (manual step input-british): --fix never writes defaults
gh-auth|PAUL||GitHub CLI signed in (gh auth status) — manual step gh-auth. Check-only: --fix never runs gh auth login
1password-cli|PAUL||1Password CLI — manual step 1password-cli. Missing app or CLI is a warning. op whoami success is signed in. Otherwise op account list is piped into a counter inside the timeout and only the account count is kept (not stored in a shell variable, a log, or a temp file; no ids, emails, UUIDs, or URLs). One or more accounts is ok and the step is not shown. No account is a warning (turn on Integrate with 1Password CLI, then run op signin). --fix never runs op
tailscale-signin|PAUL||Tailscale sign-in — manual step tailscale-signin. Reads status --json only (Running and LoginName paul.done@anysphere.co). --fix never signs in and never prints auth keys or node keys
finder-favorites|PAUL||Finder sidebar Favorites compared with lib/sidebar-favorites.list by reading FavoriteItems.sfl4 (or sfl3/sfl2). Check-only: writing the sidebar file is not reliable, and mysides is not a Homebrew formula or cask, so --fix never changes Favorites
finder-sidebar|PAUL||Finder sidebar rows named in the top sidebar section and FavoriteVolumes (Shared, AirDrop and iCloud Drive hidden, home / Macintosh HD / Network / Trash visible). Check-only: --fix never writes those files. A row the files do not name stays by hand. No tags in the sidebar is manual step finder-sidebar-tags. FavoriteTagNames is not read and is not a warning
spotlight-results|PAUL||Spotlight → Results from Apps: the apps in lib/spotlight-apps.list should be off (App Store, Calculator, Dictionary, and System Settings stay on). EnabledPreferenceRules is the row list, not the on/off state, so this is check by hand, not a warning. --fix never writes Spotlight
wallpaper|PAUL||Desktop picture Tahoe Night (Landscape), asset CF6347E2-4F81-4410-8892-4830991B6C5A in the wallpaper store. Check-only: it is a wallpaper-catalog asset, not a file System Events can select, and the wallpaper store is not written. --fix never changes the picture
remove-widgets|PAUL||Placed desktop widgets, not the hide flag. widgets.instances in ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.notificationcenterui/Data/Library/Preferences/com.apple.notificationcenterui.plist (one data blob per widget). StandardHideWidgets only hides them; they still appear when the desktop is revealed. Check-only: --fix never writes that plist and never kills NotificationCenter or chronod. Remove each widget by hand (manual step remove-widgets)
user-picture|PAUL||Account picture is the Dog. SHA-256 in lib/user-picture.sha256, from the JPEGPhoto on the user account. Check-only: --fix never changes the picture
mdm|PAUL||MDM / company-managed — Fleet Self service (Fleet Desktop menu bar → My device) or IT. A missing app is a warning. --fix does not install it
security|PAUL||security setting (FileVault, firewall stealth mode, automatic security updates, SSH agent and ~/.ssh modes; git commit signing only when commit.gpgsign is on) — never changed automatically
software-update|PAUL||a pending macOS update has been waiting more than 7 days — System Settings → General → Software Update. The check reads the local Software Update plist and does not call softwareupdate
broken-symlink|PAUL||a symlink under ~/.config, ~/Library/LaunchAgents, or a home dotfile points into the dotfiles repo but the target is missing — restore it from git or re-run install.sh. --fix does not relink these
hammerspoon-config|PAUL||Hammerspoon's repo config did not compile — fix the Lua under hammerspoon/. --fix does not reload or rewrite it
launchagent-template|PAUL||a com.pdone.* LaunchAgent does not match its repo template once @HOME@ is expanded, or an installed plist is stale or unknown. This sweep only reports. The pin agents' own drift is still the SAFE launchagent fixer
delete-files|PAUL||deleting files is never automated
dotfiles-git|PAUL||dotfiles git state — no automatic commits / pushes / pulls (dotpush)
launchagent-exit|PAUL||a LaunchAgent's last run failed — read its log
health|PAUL||Mac health signal (battery, disk, memory, storage, crashes, uptime) — report only
tooling|PAUL||a tool macconfig-check.sh needs is missing or failed — install / fix it by hand
